Q5. Predict the output.

class Test {
    static void hello() {
        System.out.println("Hi");
    }
}

// inside main
Test t = null;

t.hello();

A. Hi
B. NullPointerException
C. Compilation error
D. Nothing is printed and no exception occurs

ANSWER: A. Hi

Explanation: Static methods belong to the class, so calling a static method through a null reference does not cause NullPointerException.


