Q13. Predict the output.

static void f(int a, int[] b, String s) {
    a = 5;
    b[0] = 5;
    s = "new";
}

// inside main
int a = 1;
int[] b = { 1 };
String s = "old";

f(a, b, s);

System.out.println(a + " " + b[0] + " " + s);

A. 5 5 new
B. 1 5 old
C. 1 1 old
D. 5 1 new

ANSWER: B. 1 5 old

Explanation: Java passes everything by value; changing the array object's content is visible, but changing local references/values is not.


